invariant: INV-14
file: handshake_auth.c
catches: webpki_auth_test
reason: a P-384 leaf key goes to the P-256 verifier, which reads 64 of
  its 96 bytes as a point and 32 of the 48 digest bytes. Every P-384
  signature then fails, and a client that falls back would be
  authenticating under a key nobody holds. bin/webpki_auth_test's
  p384_sha384 row objects.

--- old
    if (leaf->alg == WEBPKI_KEY_P384) {
        return p384_ecdsa_verify(leaf->key, signed_hash, sig, sig_len);
    }
--- new
    if (leaf->alg == WEBPKI_KEY_P384) {
        return p256_ecdsa_verify(leaf->key, signed_hash, sig, sig_len);
    }
